@@ -0,0 +1,31 @@
+| ID | Behavior | Spec reference | How to verify | Code | Evidence | Status |
+|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
+| I-1 | Each ordered step carries a stable ID, era, title, caption and scene; displayed numbering follows its position. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Scene step model” | Unit/component tests for step metadata and numbering after insertion, removal and reorder. | `src/presentation-kit/types.ts`, `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx` | `resolve-kit-final.log`: clamps a mounted presentation after removal and derives numbering after insertion; derives display numbers from current order | verified |
+| I-2 | Strongly typed grouped payloads pass through the presentation boundary without casts. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Scene step model” | Compile a typed grouped-scene fixture with the TypeScript build. | `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/Talk.tsx`, `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx` | `resolve-verify.log`: npm run verify invokes the TypeScript build of the typed grouped presentation | verified |
+| I-3 | Continuing entities retain identity and morph; newcomers enter after continuing motion and departing entities exit. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Stable entities morph across steps” | Component tests for identity, transition configuration and entry/exit timing; inspect motion and layout configuration. | `src/presentation-kit/nodes.tsx`, `constants.ts` | `resolve-targeted.log`: preserves layout identity and configures entry after layout and exit; `resolve-grouped-inspection.log`: layout and transition configuration | verified |
+| I-4 | Adjacent steps with the same group and scene update the existing instance; continuing entities do not get newcomer fades, and intentional stacking is preserved. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Persistent grouped scenes” | Component test tracking scene mounts and payload updates; inspect grouped entity and positioning implementation. | `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx`, `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/Talk.tsx` | `resolve-kit-final.log`: retains a grouped scene instance as payload changes; `resolve-grouped-inspection.log`: grouped entities and coordinates | verified |
+| I-5 | Kit primitives and chrome expose stable class, style and data hooks, support literal coordinates and raw motion elements, and impose no visual defaults or required styling framework. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Style ownership boundary” | Component tests for hooks and style forwarding; inspect kit and scaffold styles and dependencies; INT-001 checks materialized style neutrality. | `src/presentation-kit/nodes.tsx`, `skills/presentation/templates/bootstrap/` | `resolve-targeted.log`: forwards identity, class, style and data hooks through wrappers; `resolve-kit-final.log`: forwards class, style, identity and data hooks; INT-001 materializes bootstrap and preserves kit parity in `resolve-bootstrap-retest.log`; `resolve-style-inspection.log` | verified |
+| I-6 | Default bottom-right attribution links to the and-scene GitHub repository with the specified label and styling hook; top-left branding is opt-in. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Kit attribution” | Component tests for default attribution, link, hook, placement and absence of default header branding; inspect host branding option. | `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx` | `resolve-kit-final.log`: honors the default attribution and optional brand; shows linked attribution without default header branding | verified |
+| I-7 | Present mode shows marker and title while hiding caption, ToC and prev/next; browse mode shows title, caption, wide ToC, controls and progress; initial mode is configurable and toggling preserves position. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Present and browse modes” | Component tests for each mode, viewport-dependent ToC, initial mode and position-preserving toggle. | `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx`, `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/style.css` | `resolve-kit-final.log`: switches chrome without changing the current step; lead ruling in `acceptance-assumptions.md`: rendered viewport visibility awaits independent acceptance | not verified |
+| I-8 | Right, Space and PageDown advance; Left and PageUp go back; horizontal swipes navigate in the expected direction without intercepting keys on focused controls. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Step navigation” | Navigation hook/component tests for keys, focused interactive controls and both swipe directions. | `src/presentation-kit/usePresentationNav.ts` | `resolve-kit-final.log`: leaves navigation keys to ARIA slider and combobox controls; focused control, keyboard and swipe tests | verified |
+| I-9 | Progress controls jump to steps, ToC entries jump to the first step of their era, and active controls expose semantic current state and stable active hooks. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Step navigation” | Component tests for direct jumps, era mapping, semantic state and active hooks. | `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx` | `resolve-kit-final.log`: gives era and progress controls current-state semantics; jumps and exposes active state | verified |
+| I-10 | Navigation clamps at the first and last steps without wrapping. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Boundary behavior” | Navigation unit tests at both boundaries. | `src/presentation-kit/usePresentationNav.ts` | `resolve-kit-final.log`: exposes metadata and clamped keyboard navigation | verified |
+| I-11 | The default 880 × 380 canvas scales uniformly to available space without internal reflow, using mode-specific fit geometry. | specs/evolving-scene-presentations/spec.md, “Fixed-canvas fit scaling” | Unit tests for fit calculations at multiple viewport sizes and modes; inspect canvas dimensions and transform layout. | `src/presentation-kit/useFitScale.ts`, `constants.ts`, `Presentation.tsx` | `resolve-kit-final.log`: calculates fit in both modes including floor and cap; `scale-inspection.log`: canvas geometry | verified |
+| I-12 | The skill gathers missing topic, style and per-step content and visuals one question at a time, permits partial detail, skips redundant questions for complete prompts, and may use selective ASCII mockups. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Interactive requirement gathering” | Inspect the skill procedure for each required branch and optional mockup guidance. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | Inspected skill procedure: `skill-inspection-12.txt` | verified |
+| I-13 | The skill detects build, scene-kit and index anchors by contract, reuses existing anchors, scaffolds only missing ones, and installs required dependencies without assuming they exist. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Self-bootstrapping scaffold” | Inspect skill instructions for full, partial and already-scaffolded branches; INT-001 materializes and checks anchors and dependencies. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md`, `skills/presentation/templates/bootstrap/` | INT-001 materializes bootstrap and preserves kit parity in `resolve-bootstrap-retest.log`; `skill-and-style-inspection.log`: anchor detection and scaffold procedure | verified |
+| I-14 | Standalone or empty targets use the root; monorepos use a self-contained presentations directory; non-empty projects missing kit or index require the stated target and confirmation before scaffolding. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Self-bootstrapping scaffold” | Inspect skill target detection, resolution and confirmation instructions. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | Inspected skill procedure: `skill-inspection-14.txt` | verified |
+| I-15 | Bootstrap and presentation templates resolve relative to the skill file, independent of caller working directory; scaffold has no required framework or presentation style defaults. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Self-bootstrapping scaffold” | Inspect template resolution and scaffold files; INT-001 exercises materialization outside the repository, dependency completeness, style neutrality and kit parity. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md`, `skills/presentation/templates/` | INT-001 materializes bootstrap and preserves kit parity in `resolve-bootstrap-retest.log`; `skill-and-style-inspection.log`: template resolution and style ownership | verified |
+| I-16 | New presentations occupy their own folder and route, register alongside existing presentations, preserve existing content, and own their styling using plain CSS by default unless the host or user chooses a framework. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Create a new presentation” | Inspect skill creation and registration instructions and templates; unit tests for registry routing and coexistence. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md`, `src/main.tsx`, `src/presentations/index.ts` | `resolve-targeted.log`: lists all registered presentations on landing and loads a selected registered route; `creation-inspection.log`: creation procedure | verified |
+| I-17 | Ambiguous modification targets are listed and selected before edits; identified modifications ask only about requested changes and stay scoped. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Modify an existing presentation” | Inspect skill modification procedure for target selection, questions and edit scope. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | Inspected skill procedure: `skill-inspection-17.txt` | verified |
+| I-18 | Before reporting success the skill builds, renders at least the first step without errors, checks first, last and dense/key compositions and narrow viewports when sensitive, and fixes and rechecks failures. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Self-verify before reporting completion” | Inspect skill verification and repair instructions. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | Inspected skill procedure: `skill-inspection-18.txt` | verified |
+| I-19 | Generated presentations provide captions, next/previous navigation and the evolving-scene model; their build and first render are checked. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Generated presentation quality bar” | Inspect generation and verification instructions and templates; component tests for caption and navigation contracts; E2E-001 checks the reference build and render. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md`, `src/presentation-kit/Presentation.tsx`, `skills/presentation/templates/presentation/` | `resolve-kit-final.log`: exposes metadata and clamped keyboard navigation; `creation-inspection.log`: skill and templates; E2E-001: `resolve-verify.log` | verified |
+| I-20 | Visual review checks canvas fit, readable intentional overlaps and chrome collisions; local screenshot helper is preferred or temporary helper stays under project root; warnings are reviewed, accidental defects fixed and only readable intentional overlaps marked. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Generated presentation quality bar” | Inspect skill visual-review, helper selection, warning repair and overlap-marker instructions. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md` | Inspected skill procedure: `skill-inspection-20.txt` | verified |
+| I-21 | Active navigation is visually distinct and attribution legible through presentation or host CSS, while the kit remains visually neutral. | specs/presentation-skill/spec.md, “Generated presentation quality bar” | Inspect skill styling instructions and ownership of sample and kit CSS; INT-002 checks advisory diagnostics for indistinct chrome and attribution. | `skills/presentation/SKILL.md`, `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/style.css` | `resolve-style-inspection.log`: presentation-owned styling; INT-002 emits settled screenshots and advisory diagnostics in `resolve-browser-last.log` | verified |
+| I-22 | Verification builds the whole application and fails on type or build errors with a clear phase and nonzero exit. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Build verification”; “Pass/fail reporting” | E2E-001 checks successful whole-app verification; E2E-002 injects a build failure and checks reporting and exit status. | `scripts/verify.mjs` | E2E-001 `npm run verify` in `resolve-verify.log`; E2E-002 build failure names its phase in `resolve-browser-focused.log`; E2E-002 reports build, missing sample, browser and transition failures in `resolve-browser-last.log` | verified |
+| I-23 | The registered, reachable reference sample has the specified nine eras, titles and captions in order; missing or malformed sample fails verification. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Committed reference sample” | E2E-001 checks registration, route and ordered normative metadata; E2E-002 checks missing and out-of-order failure. | `scripts/verify.mjs`, `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/Talk.tsx` | E2E-001 `npm run verify` in `resolve-verify.log`; E2E-002 reports build, missing sample, browser and transition failures in `resolve-browser-last.log`, including reversed steps | verified |
+| I-24 | The sample is one accumulating scene with the nine specified visual intents, including conversation, cards and morph links, depth control, kit socket, verification node, modify arc and reveal frame, without rearranging existing entities. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Committed reference sample” | Inspect sample scene data, entity identities, coordinates and step composition against the nine normative scene descriptions. | `src/presentations/how-to-make-a-presentation/Talk.tsx`, `style.css` | `resolve-sample.log`: source inspection of tray, question position, dock and verification link; `resolve-grouped-inspection.log`: full sample composition | verified |
+| I-25 | Production verification traverses every sample step through public count/index hooks, uses 127.0.0.1 for preview, readiness and navigation, and reports success clearly. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Render verification”; “Pass/fail reporting” | E2E-001 exercises the production browser verification path and its success output. | `scripts/verify.mjs` | E2E-001 `npm run verify` in `resolve-verify.log`: production build and nine-step traversal | verified |
+| I-26 | Console errors, uncaught page errors, render errors and failed transitions fail verification with the offending step and phase; preview processes are cleaned up on failure. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Render verification”; “Pass/fail reporting” | E2E-002 injects browser and transition faults and checks nonzero exit, step-specific reporting and subprocess cleanup; inspect error handlers for both console and page errors. | `scripts/verify.mjs` | E2E-002 reports build, missing sample, browser and transition failures in `resolve-browser-last.log`, including scene-render exception and cleanup; `resolve-script-inspection.log` | verified |
+| I-27 | The project-local helper captures every registered presentation step at a standard desktop size in a predictable local directory after the configured animation settle interval. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Visual inspection artifacts” | INT-002 runs the production-preview helper and checks screenshot count, location and settling. | `scripts/inspect-presentation.mjs` | INT-002 emits settled screenshots and advisory diagnostics in `resolve-browser-last.log`, including focused input and distinct step indices | verified |
+| I-28 | The helper warns with step and element details for unmarked visible text/chrome collisions, exempts marked subtrees, and advises on indistinct active progress or ToC and undersized or browser-default attribution. | specs/presentation-verification/spec.md, “Visual inspection artifacts” | INT-002 exercises collision, allowed overlap, active chrome and attribution diagnostic variants; inspect warning messages for actionable hooks and step details. | `scripts/inspect-presentation.mjs` | INT-002 emits settled screenshots and advisory diagnostics in `resolve-browser-last.log`, including mixed text, exemptions and separate attribution cases; `resolve-script-inspection.log` | verified |
+| I-29 | Bootstrap snapshot stays aligned with canonical non-test kit files, and scaffolded verification and inspection scripts match their repository counterparts. | design.md, “Repository layout”; “Verification” | INT-001 compares kit files; compare root and bootstrap script copies byte-for-byte. | `src/presentation-kit/`, `skills/presentation/templates/bootstrap/`, `scripts/` | INT-001 materializes bootstrap and preserves kit parity in `resolve-bootstrap-retest.log`; `resolve-parity.log`: kit and script comparisons | verified |
